/* ============================================================
   Answer It - Arabic locale bank for the curated core
   ============================================================
   Hand-written translations of every question in bank/curated-core.js. This is tier 0 of the
   translation chain (see translateQuestion() in index.html): a curated question shown in AR
   never touches a translation service at all - no latency, no quota, no network, and it works
   from file://. The live chain (Worker -> MyMemory -> English) only ever handles the ~40% of a
   round that comes from the APIs.

   Shape: keyed by the EXACT English question text from curated-core.js.
     "<english question>": { t: "<translated question>", o: { "<english option>": "<translated>" } }
   The `o` map covers every option - correct and wrong alike - because options are shuffled at
   load time, so a positional array would not survive. A missing key simply falls through to the
   next tier, which is why a partial edit here can never break a round.

   Proper nouns are transliterated into Arabic script (Nizar's call, 2026-08-26):
   "Pink Floyd" -> "بينك فلويد" - not left in Latin, and not glossed in brackets.

   Edit freely: this file is the source of truth, not generated output. Run `node check.mjs` at
   the repo root afterwards - it validates coverage, option parity and post-translation option
   collisions. index.html loads this lazily the first time AR is selected, so English
   players never download it.
   ============================================================ */
